# GitHub agent workflow

Config: `.github/agent-workflow.yml`. Skills: `~/.cursor/skills/gh-{issues,ship,release,roadmap-sync}/`.

**Do not edit** `.cursor/skills/10x-*` for GitHub/Kanban hooks — `10x get` overwrites those. Put durable behavior here and in `gh-*` skills instead.

## Route by intent

| User intent | Skill |
|-------------|--------|
| Implement / fix / refactor / enhance | **`gh-issues`** before coding (English issues + labels) |
| Push / PR / merge **without** production deploy | **`gh-ship`** |
| Deploy / release / tag from any branch | **`gh-release` once** (embeds ship → tag → CD → close) |
| Sync roadmap → board / `/gh-roadmap-sync` | **`gh-roadmap-sync`** |

Production from a feature branch: **`/gh-release`** only (no separate `/gh-ship`).

## After `/10x-roadmap` (mandatory ask)

When `context/foundation/roadmap.md` was just generated or regenerated in this session, **after** the roadmap handoff summary, ask (do not auto-run):

> Map roadmap items to the Kanban board now?
> - Yes → read and run **`gh-roadmap-sync`**
> - No → skip; user can run `/gh-roadmap-sync` later

This ask lives here on purpose so 10x updates to `10x-roadmap` cannot remove it.

## Hard gates

- No commit / push / PR / merge / tag unless the user asked.
- Never merge while CI is pending or failing (`gh pr checks`).
- Issues: English; one type label (`bug`|`enhancement`|`documentation`); add `foundation`|`slice`|`north-star` when roadmap-mapped.
- Kanban only via `~/.cursor/skills/gh-issues/scripts/kanban-*.sh` (or `gh-roadmap-sync` script).
- `cd_trigger: tag` — merge to `main` ≠ deploy; production = `/gh-release`.
- After implementation: English comment **and** Kanban **In review** same turn.

## Branching (trunk)

`fix/*` or `feature/*` from up-to-date `main`; PR target `main`.
